== {{Dlc+|r}} Pill Classes ==
[[Repentance]] introduces the mechanic of pill classes. Internally, pills are given a class from 0 to 3 and a polarity that reflects their influence:

Pills in class 0 have little to no impact on a run overall, while pills in higher classes are correspondingly more influential, class 3 pills having effects as significant as permanent stat changes.
Classes that end with + or - denote a positive or negative effect, otherwise considered neutral.

This mechanic is used to balance the pill pool and avoid having too many negative or positive pills. Polarity is used by certain items to determine which pills to convert.

{{dlc-}}

== {{dlc+|r}} Gold Pills ==
[[Repentance]] introduces '''Gold Pills''' (or Golden Pills). Using one gives a random pill effect. Gold pills are unique in that they can be used multiple times, with each use only having a 10% chance to remove the pill. This often allows many uses before they finally disappear.

* Unlocked by: {{achievement unlock|Gold Pill}}.
* The possible effects are all effects that aren't in the run's pill pool, which means if you see an effect from a normal pill, you will never see it from a gold pill.
* Items such as {{I|PHD}} or {{I|Lucky Foot}} which alter pill effects also work on the effects of this pill, allowing many beneficial effects to be stacked with little risk. Effects altered by these items may overlap with the effects in the run's pill pool; for example, a run might have Tears Up in the pill pool and Tears Down outside of the pill pool, which will be turned into Tears Up due to the effects of the item.
* Gold Pills have an ID of 5.70.14.
* A Gold Pill can also be a Horse Pill. Gold Horse Pills use the Horse Pill effect on every use.
* Gold horse pills are most likely the rarest pickup in the game with a 0.06% chance of spawning instead of a normal pill.
* If a Gold Pill uses the 'Vurp' effect, and no other pill was used prior, another gold pill will drop.

{{dlc-}}

== {{dlc+|r}} Horse Pills ==
''[[Repentance]]'' introduces '''Horse Pills'''. These are larger versions of the standard pills with a more powerful effect, but only appear very rarely. Unique sound effects can be heard when they are used, and the narrator's normal spoken voice lines are instead shouted using a different voice.

* Unlocked by: {{achievement unlock|Horse Pill}}.
* All items that work with pills work identically with horse pills.
* A horse pill with a given effect has the same color as the normal pill does.
* Horse pills have an ID of the normal ID + 2048 (i.e. 1 << 11). For example, a white-blue pill has an ID of 2, so the horse pill version would have an ID of 5.70.2050.
* It is also possible to have a golden horse pill. (It has an ID of 5.70.2062.)
{{dlc-}}

== Probabilities ==
Pills that spawn with a sub-type of 0 (i.e. a random pill) will have the following probabilities:

* Random normal pill - 97.86%
* Specific normal pill - 7.53%
* Gold pill - 0.7%
* Random horse pill - 1.43%
* Specific horse pill - 0.11%
* Gold horse pill - 0.01%

== Notes ==
* Among the [[attribute]]-modifying pill effects, only five of the seven [[attribute|visible attributes]] are covered: health, range, tears, speed, and luck. Both shot speed and damage can't be altered by pills.
** {{dlc|r}} Shot speed can now be altered with pills. Damage can now also be altered with pills with {{I|False PHD|dlc=x}}.
* If a "Health Up" pill is used while Isaac has 11 empty red hearts and one non-red heart, the non-red heart will be replaced with an empty container, killing Isaac.
* Having {{i|Midas' Touch}}, {{t|Meconium}}, or {{i|Hallowed Ground}} and using a "Re-Lax" pill has a chance to spawn {{E|Golden Poop}}, {{E|Black Poop}}, or {{E|White Poop}}, respectively.
* If the item {{i|PHD}} is picked up and then lost in any way, such as rerolling by the {{i|D4}} or a {{R|Dice Room}}, or dropping it as {{c|Tainted Isaac}}, pills will remain fully identified for the rest of the run, but negative pills will not be converted.
* {{dlc|a}} Pill effects have a chance to be narrated upon use, as do [[card]]s and [[rune]]s.
* {{dlc|a}} Currently, the "Retro Vision" pill effect can crash the game on some machines, resulting in restarting the current floor when the game is continued.
* {{dlc|a}} The "Addicted!" pill will have no effect if Isaac has {{i|The Wafer}}.
** Despite this, if Isaac takes both the "Addicted!" pill with "Percs!" in the same room, a full heart of damage will be taken from all sources.
* {{dlc|a}} Using an "Infested!" pill on {{E|Red Poop}} will spawn [[blue spider]]s and the Red Poop will regenerate.
* {{dlc|a}} If a Tiny or Large [[Champion]] monster drops a "One Makes You Smaller"/"Larger" pill and either pill is not in the current pill pool, an existing pill will be overwritten. If the chosen pill was already identified, the new pill will also be.
* {{dlc+|a}} "R U A Wizard" does not affect {{C|Lilith}}'s {{i|Incubus}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|a}} Isaac's hitbox can be reduced to 30% of original, which is achieved after 6 One Makes You Small pills. Further pills will only make him visually smaller, with no additional benefit.
* {{dlc|a+}} Using a "Gulp!" pill while holding two [[trinket]]s (with {{i|Belly Button}} or {{i|Mom's Purse}}) will cause both trinkets to be absorbed.
* {{c|Magdalene}}'s starting pill will override one of the pills in the current run's pill set if it doesn't exist in it ("Speed Up" for ''Afterbirth+'', or "Full Health" in ''Repentance''). The pill that is converted is dependent on the run's seed.
** This only applies if the run is started as Magdalene, not if Isaac turns into Magdalene using {{i|Clicker}}.
* {{dlc|r}} All golden pills in the run have a shared sequence of effects they activate, so reversing the effects of one golden pill through {{i|Glowing Hourglass}} and consuming another golden pill will activate the same effects.
* {{dlc|r}} If a "Vurp!" effect is activated by a golden pill, it will spawn the last non-golden pill taken by Isaac, or a golden pill if no non-golden pills have been taken by Isaac in the run.
** A normal "Vurp!" pill will also ignore previous effects granted by gold pills.
* {{dlc|r}} If a [[Rocks#Marked Skulls|Marked Skull]] is destroyed while Isaac is holding {{i|Little Baggy}}, it will spawn a "Telepill" instead of {{p|0 - The Fool}}. If "Telepills" doesn't exist in the current run's pill set, an existing pill will be overwritten. The pill that is converted is dependent on the run's seed.
* {{dlc+|r}} While transformed into {{C|The Lost}} form (for example, by a {{e|White Fire Place}}), "Health Down" pills turn into "Health Up" pills, and "Bad Trip" pills become "Full Health", regardless of Isaac's health.{{dlc-}}
* "Telepills" is unobtainable in [[Greed Mode]].
** {{dlc|r+}} The "Amnesia" and "???" pills are also unobtainable in Greed Mode.

== Strategy ==
* {{dlc|r}} There are 24 good effects, 14 neutral (sometimes good/sometimes bad) effects, and 12 negative effects. This means that taking mystery pills is usually beneficial.
* Use of unidentified pills is recommended for outside of combat as Hematemesis, R U a Wizard?, Paralysis, {{dlc|a}}Addicted!, {{dlc|a+}} X-Lax, and {{dlc|a+}} I'm Excited!!! can be detrimental mid-fight. However, {{dlc|a+}} I'm Drowsy..., {{dlc|a+}} Something's wrong..., Lemon Party, Bad Gas, and Pheromones are useless outside of combat.
* {{dlc|a}} Percs! can be used in the {{R|Sacrifice Room}} to reduce the damage Isaac takes, potentially allowing him to do more sacrifices. However, if Isaac is teleported to the Devil/Angel room, he loses the effect.
* {{dlc|a}} The invincibility effect from Power Pill and {{dlc|a+}} Feels like I'm walking on sunshine! can be utilized to get into {{R|Curse Room}}s, play {{Machine|Blood Donation Machine}}s and {{Machine|Confessional}}s, or use {{Machine|Devil Beggar}}s and {{Machine|Hell Game}}s without taking any damage.
** {{dlc|a}} Percs! can be used to reduce damage from these from [[chapter 4]] onward.
* {{dlc|r}}{{t|Endless Nameless|n}} can be used to effectively generate infinite golden pills, as the trinket's ability to respawn collectibles applies with every use.
* {{dlc|r}} Taking only golden pills in a run can allow for infinite golden pill generation by repeatedly activating the Vurp! effect.
* {{dlc|r+}} ??? can be distinguished from unidentified pills more easily by enabling item descriptions in the Options menu. They will display as "???" instead of "Unidentified Pill" when approached.

