== Trivia ==
* {{dlc|a+}} The Vurp! pill is a portmanteau of the words vomit and burp.
* {{dlc|a}} Power Pills activating the Gamekid effect is a reference to Pac-Man, in which the "Super-Pac" powerup is obtained by eating a Power Pellet.
* "I Found Pills (and Ate Them)," "R U a Wizard?," and "I can see Forever" are all [[wikipedia:image macro|image macro]] memes.
* {{dlc|a+}} The Feels like I'm walking on sunshine! pill is a reference to the 80s song [[wikipedia:Walking on Sunshine (Katrina and the Waves song)|Walking on Sunshine]].
** Furthermore, creator Edmund McMillen made in 2010 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eMIXDlvD_Yw a video with the same name], although it doesn't feature the actual Walking on Sunshine song.
* Balls of Steel is a reference to ''Duke Nukem''; it is one of Duke's more famous quotes.
* Explosive Diarrhea is extremely loud and forceful [[wikipedia:diarrhea|diarrhea]]. In the original game, the message that displayed when the pill was activated was "Oh No!". The pill name and effect are likely a reference to Atomic Bomberman where a pickup of the same name would cause the player to drop bombs behind them uncontrollably for a short duration.
* Shot speed effects were introduced in The Binding of Isaac: Eternal Edition, after the release of Rebirth. They were finally added to Rebirth in the Repentance DLC.
* Hematemesis is a medical term for [https://muschealth.org/medical-services/ddc/patients/symptoms-and-conditions/hematemesis vomiting blood].
* Lemon Party is a reference to internet shock site featuring a group of elderly men performing oral sex, peeing on each other.
* "Puberty" having a negative sound effect is a tongue in cheek connotation to how unpleasant that period in life can be.
* {{dlc|a}} Friends Till the End! was originally in the Wrath of the Lamb but removed in Rebirth, then put back into Afterbirth.
* {{dlc|ana+}} Friends Till The End! is the only non-narrated pill.
* 48 Hour Energy is a reference to the drink 5 Hour Energy.
* {{dlc|a+}} X-Lax is a reference to the anti-constipation medicine Ex-Lax.
* {{dlc|a}} "One makes you larger" and "One makes you small" are references to Alice in Wonderland, and the specific wording is a reference to the song White Rabbit by Jefferson Airplane.
* {{dlc|a}} "Percs" is a reference to a street name for the prescription drug Percocet, which is more generically known as Oxycodone. This drug is meant to be used to treat pain, but it is often abused for recreational purposes.
* {{dlc|a}} The "???" is the only pill that has 3 different narrated voice lines.
* {{dlc|a+}} "I'm Drowsy..." and "I'm Excited!!!" are references to benzodiazepines and stimulants respectively. From the pill themed Mom items, it's implied that Mom is a drug addict, and therefore keeps narcotics around the home and in her coin purse.
* {{dlc|r}} "Horse pills" is a slang term used to refer to large, hard to swallow pills, hence their sprites being larger than those of regular pills.

